    "description": "The allocation census has fired three times and each time removed the dominant term; after a +150.8% win, allocation is likely no longer the top cost. Run a perf record/report (and a second LD_PRELOAD census for comparison) over the same 2000-run VR bench on merged HEAD, and report the top-20 self-time symbols plus the residual >=1032-byte allocation histogram side by side in research/observations/. Then apply the standard lever to the single largest remaining cost center in spur-core/src/simulator/core (exec.rs, scheduler.rs, state.rs) or spur-core/src/interpreter: hoist an inner-loop clone, replace a per-step HashMap lookup with an index, or shrink a hot struct, pinning size_of or an operation count with a unit test. No config field gates this; executions must stay byte-identical per seed. Falsifier: no single symbol carries enough self time for a 5% bench delta.",
